        "question": "What are the primary differences in clinical diagnostic accuracy between Med-PaLM 2 and standard GPT-4?",
        "answer": "Based on the indexed literature, **Med-PaLM 2** was explicitly instruction-tuned on specialized clinical QA benchmarks (HealthSearchQA, LiveQA, MedicationQA) and evaluated on USMLE-style questions in MedQA, where it achieved an accuracy of **86.5%**, surpassing prior state-of-the-art models by over 18%.\n\nIn contrast, **GPT-4** was evaluated primarily in operational clinic workflows (SOAP note generation and patient messaging) rather than standalone board examinations in these papers. In note generation, GPT-4 demonstrated equivalent completeness (4.6/5.0) to human physicians, but exhibited a **4.2% hallucination error rate** requiring clinician oversight. Physician panel reviews of Med-PaLM 2 answers reported a **92.9% consensus alignment** with accepted medical guidelines.",
