        "answer": "The surveyed literature highlights three core mechanisms to counteract hallucinations in clinical notes:\n\n1. **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)**: Rostova et al. (2024) demonstrated across 78 trials that grounding LLM outputs against verified clinical guideline vector stores reduces factual hallucination rates from **14.2% down to 2.8%**.\n\n2. **Clinician-in-the-Loop Co-Pilot Protocols**: Chen et al. (2024) showed that mandatory attending physician sign-off caught all 51 hallucinated negative findings during outpatient trials, while still preserving a net **48% time savings**.\n\n3. **Structured Template Constrained Decoding**: Forcing outputs into strict SOAP sections with negative finding assertions only permitted when explicitly evidenced in the encounter audio or transcript.",
